1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:02,794
[dramatic music]

2
00:00:02,794 --> 00:00:04,129
[Bonzle] Any clue
what they're saying?

3
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:06,215
How would I know?
I can't read lips.

4
00:00:06,215 --> 00:00:08,926
They look upset. Why?

5
00:00:08,926 --> 00:00:11,136
-Again, how would I--
-Where are they going?

6
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,387
They're not going...

7
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:13,639
Oh, wait, they are.

8
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:17,559
Nice! Let's give
this another shot.

9
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:22,773
[dramatic music]

10
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:23,899
Let's go, everyone.

11
00:00:23,899 --> 00:00:25,526
[sighing]

12
00:00:26,318 --> 00:00:29,279
You too, Wyldfyre.
Time for warm-ups.

13
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:31,990
[groans] I lost my heat power.

14
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,159
I've literally got
nothing to warm up with!

15
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:38,080
There's more to being a
Ninja than Elemental Powers.

16
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:42,209
Yeah, like sleeping in.
Don't ninja sleep in?

17
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:46,046
You need to focus on
learning Spinjitzu.

18
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:47,172
[grumbling]

19
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:48,924
[Riyu yawns]

20
00:00:52,928 --> 00:00:55,180
I know you'll find Jay, Nya.

21
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:58,642
I have to. Even if he doesn't
remember anything about us,

22
00:00:58,642 --> 00:01:00,435
Jay belongs with us.

23
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:02,229
His family.

24
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:04,064
But I'm scared, Lloyd.

25
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:07,693
He shattered his goodness.
What if he can't heal it?

26
00:01:07,693 --> 00:01:09,486
There has to be a way.

27
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:11,655
And we'll all join you as
soon as the tournament ends

28
00:01:11,655 --> 00:01:14,366
and we find out whoever's behind
the attacks on the dragons.

29
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:15,367
Be careful.

30
00:01:17,369 --> 00:01:19,329
You too. We'll miss you.

31
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:23,834
[sighs]

32
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:28,714
I could really use my
older brother right now.

33
00:01:29,548 --> 00:01:32,342
I'd do anything to hear
your voice again, Kai.

34
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,344
[Kai] Hello? Are you there?

35
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:35,888
Kai?

36
00:01:35,888 --> 00:01:37,097
[Riyu squeals]

37
00:01:37,097 --> 00:01:39,474
Riyu, did you hear him too?

38
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:41,059
[Riyu roars]

39
00:01:41,059 --> 00:01:43,687
[Kai] Riyu, is someone with you?

40
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:46,106
Kai! Kai, can you hear me?

41
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:50,235
[Kai] I said, Riyu, if there's
someone there let me know!

42
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,445
He can't hear me?

43
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:55,699
-There must be some way to--
-[light zaps]

44
00:01:55,699 --> 00:01:57,075
[Kai] We might not
have much time.

45
00:01:57,951 --> 00:01:59,369
Kai?

46
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:00,954
Nya! Nya, is that you?

47
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,664
You have a sister
I don't know about?

48
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,499
How are you talking
through this stone?

49
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:06,668
"Stone"? I don't know.

50
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,378
I've got some of Riyu's
scales stuck to me,

51
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:10,130
so Bonzle thinks the
physical connection

52
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:11,548
lets us communicate.

53
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,509
Dunno why it works
with you, though.

54
00:02:13,509 --> 00:02:17,262
You're my brother. We share
a lot more than a few scales.

55
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:19,640
The Forbidden Five,
four, whatever,

56
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,725
they're also talking to
someone on the outside.

57
00:02:21,725 --> 00:02:23,143
Probably planning
something terrible.

58
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:25,145
[Nya] Great, more bad news.

59
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,563
Let me guess, wherever you are,

60
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:27,981
the world's in danger again?

61
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:31,318
Kai, I found Jay.
Only he's not our Jay.

62
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:35,614
He lost his memory.
It's like he's a completely
different person.

63
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:39,409
In Jay's case, that might
be an improvement. Ha!

64
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:41,745
Save the jokes till
after we free you.

65
00:02:42,454 --> 00:02:45,791
Maybe this stone could do
more than allow us to speak.

66
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:48,168
It could potentially
open a doorway out.

67
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:49,753
[door bangs]

68
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:52,130
Nya, Nya, are you there?

69
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:55,342
What happened?
Nya!

70
00:02:55,342 --> 00:02:58,178
♪ Lost in the unknown
So much to see ♪

71
00:02:58,178 --> 00:03:01,306
♪ Together we will rise ♪

72
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:04,434
♪ We fight ♪

73
00:03:04,434 --> 00:03:07,604
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

74
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:10,315
[fire roars]

75
00:03:12,109 --> 00:03:15,195
[yawns] It took me forever
to get back to sleep.

76
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:18,407
Every time I closed my eyes
I saw that monastery again.

77
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:22,286
Why now? Why me?
Why is it here?

78
00:03:22,286 --> 00:03:24,538
Perhaps rather than
asking why you were guided

79
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:26,999
to a mysterious monastery
in the middle of the night,

80
00:03:26,999 --> 00:03:30,169
a better line of inquiry might
be how you could reach it.

81
00:03:37,134 --> 00:03:38,886
I need a hot bath.

82
00:03:38,886 --> 00:03:42,055
-You're back.
-Arin, where've you been?

83
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:43,932
You were gone again
when we woke up.

84
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:46,977
I had stuff to think over.

85
00:03:46,977 --> 00:03:49,438
[somber music]

86
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:51,273
Right, the detective work.

87
00:03:51,273 --> 00:03:53,025
Did you find something
in Ras's dorm?

88
00:03:53,025 --> 00:03:56,320
No. Ras caught Riyu and me.

89
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,362
[group gasps]

90
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:59,364
How'd you escape? Smoke bomb?

91
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,284
I really thought being
a Ninja would involve

92
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:04,328
way more smoke bombs.

93
00:04:04,328 --> 00:04:05,787
Ras let us go.

94
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:08,332
Ras? Ras Ras?

95
00:04:08,332 --> 00:04:09,875
Are we talking about
the same Ras here?

96
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:12,085
Big scary Tiger-man,
hates dragons?

97
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:13,712
He let you go?

98
00:04:13,712 --> 00:04:16,924
Maybe we don't understand
his real motivation yet.

99
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:21,011
So you don't think he's
behind what happened

100
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:22,429
to the Matriarch Dragons?

101
00:04:22,429 --> 00:04:24,389
Ras is the obvious suspect.

102
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:28,310
He led the Claws of the Imperium
against a Matriarch before.

103
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:31,355
But nothing connects him
to the stolen horns yet.

104
00:04:31,355 --> 00:04:35,651
And don't forget,
Ras was also attacked by
a bot that first night.

105
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:39,279
Our past with Ras may have
created a confirmation bias

106
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,989
that blinds us to other threats.

107
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:45,369
Yeah, threats like
this ugly guy, Bleckt!

108
00:04:45,369 --> 00:04:49,581
Have you seen the
way he talks to Roby?
Total villain energy.

109
00:04:49,581 --> 00:04:53,502
Even his name sounds
like the sound you make
when you barf. Bleeckt!

110
00:04:53,502 --> 00:04:56,296
Bleckt defeating three
Matriarch-level dragons

111
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,631
seems improbable.

112
00:04:57,631 --> 00:05:00,133
Agree. And that's
a drawing of Zur.

113
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:02,553
Uh, if you say so.

114
00:05:02,553 --> 00:05:06,306
The Devonian who beat Zane?
Why would he be a suspect?

115
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:10,143
Well, I did hear rumors
back in the Crossroads

116
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:13,063
about Devonians grinding
dragon horns into a powder

117
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:15,274
they mix with food for
strength in battle.

118
00:05:15,274 --> 00:05:17,317
Dragon horns can
make you stronger,

119
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:19,570
but also fill you with rage.

120
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:21,655
Rumors and gossip
aren't evidence.

121
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:25,534
Zeatrix has been oddly confident
about winning the games.

122
00:05:25,534 --> 00:05:27,661
It's like she knows
something we don't.

123
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:29,746
And she wasn't attacked by bots,

124
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:31,456
even though she drew
a lot of attention

125
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:33,458
at the banquet
earlier that night.

126
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,294
She definitely has
a grudge against us

127
00:05:35,294 --> 00:05:36,795
for dethroning Beatrix.

128
00:05:36,795 --> 00:05:39,089
Even though we totally
did her a favor.

129
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:42,509
Psh! She's super powerful
but can't control her anger.

130
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:43,844
Huh! Pathetic.

131
00:05:45,429 --> 00:05:47,681
[dramatic music]

132
00:05:48,348 --> 00:05:50,976
Uh, Lloyd? What do you think?

133
00:05:50,976 --> 00:05:53,395
Well, Zeatrix was
once next in line

134
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:56,523
for the throne of a kingdom
that ran on Dragon Power.

135
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:59,735
If anyone knows what to do
with those horns, it's her.

136
00:05:59,735 --> 00:06:03,822
Great, we have a bunch
of suspects but no proof.

137
00:06:03,822 --> 00:06:04,990
Now what?

138
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:06,617
I still have one lead.

139
00:06:06,617 --> 00:06:08,452
I found this symbol in the area

140
00:06:08,452 --> 00:06:10,495
where the bot
attack started from.

141
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:12,539
But I have no idea
what it means.

142
00:06:12,539 --> 00:06:16,460
Hey, you should check
the Temple City Museum.

143
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:20,631
Geo and I walked through there
and saw all kinds of
ancient art and writing.

144
00:06:20,631 --> 00:06:23,091
Really? I'll go right away.

145
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:24,510
I could come with you.

146
00:06:26,929 --> 00:06:28,639
Did that feel weird to you?

147
00:06:28,639 --> 00:06:31,475
My Social Encounter
Algorithm registered

148
00:06:31,475 --> 00:06:33,352
high levels of cringe.

149
00:06:33,352 --> 00:06:36,438
Lloyd, can we talk about Arin?

150
00:06:36,438 --> 00:06:39,066
-[gasps]
-[dramatic music]

151
00:06:44,947 --> 00:06:46,406
Another vision?

152
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:48,492
I thought Rontu taught
you to control them!

153
00:06:48,492 --> 00:06:50,536
This one, so strong.

154
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:54,540
I think today's the
day I fight Zeatrix.

155
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,749
[gasps]

156
00:06:58,794 --> 00:07:00,629
And I'm going to lose.

157
00:07:00,629 --> 00:07:03,549
[dramatic music]

158
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,969
[ominous music]

159
00:07:15,352 --> 00:07:17,813
[somber music]

160
00:07:23,569 --> 00:07:26,196
[dramatic music]

161
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:29,867
No, no, no.
Oops, I mean, yes,

162
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:33,287
and make sure you capture
my broad shoulders.

163
00:07:33,287 --> 00:07:35,372
Arin! Whatdaya think?

164
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:37,541
I'm gonna replace these
boring old artifacts

165
00:07:37,541 --> 00:07:39,543
with some bold modern art.

166
00:07:39,543 --> 00:07:41,670
New and daring, like me.

167
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:45,424
The past is for dead people,
right? Can I get a stang-zoot?

168
00:07:45,424 --> 00:07:47,801
I don't know.
History can be cool.

169
00:07:47,801 --> 00:07:48,802
Hey, Geo.

170
00:07:51,138 --> 00:07:53,557
Ugh! You sound like my uncle.

171
00:07:53,557 --> 00:07:56,768
He spends hours here. And
not asleep, like you'd think.

172
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:59,938
If it were up to him, there'd be
an exhibit to watch paint dry.

173
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:02,941
Good thing ya boi's the
game Master and not him!

174
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:05,569
I see a modern,
interactive experience

175
00:08:05,569 --> 00:08:09,156
with screens everywhere.
Over there, a holo-display

176
00:08:09,156 --> 00:08:12,618
of the seven Source Dragons
locked in an epic battle.
Stang-zoot, right?

177
00:08:12,618 --> 00:08:17,664
That does sound cool.
I mean, stoot-zang, or whatever.

178
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:20,584
Right? I don't believe any of
those old dragon myths,

179
00:08:20,584 --> 00:08:23,086
but you can't beat the branding!

180
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:25,130
And this'll house
the Element Cup.

181
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:27,299
Imagine lights hitting
the glorious sheen

182
00:08:27,299 --> 00:08:29,092
of its dragon ivory.

183
00:08:29,092 --> 00:08:31,178
-Dragon ivory?
-Sure.

184
00:08:31,178 --> 00:08:33,514
The cup is made from the
polished horn of an arc dragon.

185
00:08:33,514 --> 00:08:37,059
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Arc as in a Matriarch?

186
00:08:37,059 --> 00:08:38,644
Matriarchs, Patriarchs.

187
00:08:38,644 --> 00:08:40,729
Centuries ago, people
used arc dragon horns

188
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:42,523
to amplify Elemental Powers.

189
00:08:42,523 --> 00:08:44,775
The cup's made of it, it's as
old as the games themselves.

190
00:08:44,775 --> 00:08:46,068
Let me show you where I'll build

191
00:08:46,068 --> 00:08:47,945
the VR
Experience-slash-gift shop.

192
00:08:50,239 --> 00:08:51,281
Who's that?

193
00:08:52,574 --> 00:08:55,369
My great, great, great,
great, you get the idea.

194
00:08:55,369 --> 00:08:57,246
The tournament's
first games master.

195
00:08:57,246 --> 00:08:59,122
A visionary, like me.

196
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:00,624
I'm actually wearing
his vestments.

197
00:09:00,624 --> 00:09:03,627
Tailored for max
swagger, drip-drip.

198
00:09:03,627 --> 00:09:06,630
Thought I'd throw my uncle a
bone with my outfit, at least.

199
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:11,093
Oops! Gotta go! The games won't
master themselves!

200
00:09:11,093 --> 00:09:13,470
[dramatic music]

201
00:09:18,267 --> 00:09:19,643
[gasps]

202
00:09:19,643 --> 00:09:21,061
Roby, wait!

203
00:09:21,061 --> 00:09:22,604
Sorry, duty calls.

204
00:09:24,773 --> 00:09:26,316
[gasps]

205
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:27,734
[Arin] Could the villain
I've been looking for

206
00:09:27,734 --> 00:09:30,612
this whole time be, Roby?

207
00:09:34,616 --> 00:09:36,618
Has anyone seen Riyu?

208
00:09:36,618 --> 00:09:39,246
He probably helped Nya leave
the city and got distracted

209
00:09:39,246 --> 00:09:42,207
by all the delicious
Temple City concessions.

210
00:09:42,207 --> 00:09:45,544
[dramatic music]

211
00:09:45,544 --> 00:09:48,672
Elemental Masters, are
you ready to battle?

212
00:09:48,672 --> 00:09:50,674
To entertain? To win?

213
00:09:50,674 --> 00:09:53,677
[crowd cheering]

214
00:09:53,677 --> 00:09:56,597
First up, the hard-fighting
snake who's bound

215
00:09:56,597 --> 00:09:57,848
to make you shake.

216
00:09:57,848 --> 00:10:01,310
It's Frak, the Elemental
Master of Quake!

217
00:10:01,310 --> 00:10:03,020
-[crowd cheering]
-[sighs]

218
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:06,690
Versus a descendent
of the Devonian King,

219
00:10:06,690 --> 00:10:09,443
who'll throw you
right out of the ring,

220
00:10:09,443 --> 00:10:12,905
it's Zur, the Elemental
Master of Reflex!

221
00:10:12,905 --> 00:10:15,657
[dramatic music]

222
00:10:19,077 --> 00:10:21,663
Excuse me, Master Cole, sir.

223
00:10:21,663 --> 00:10:24,708
Can I ask a question
about your Earth power?

224
00:10:24,708 --> 00:10:27,377
Uh, sure, I guess.

225
00:10:27,377 --> 00:10:29,713
I've been practicing
with it since our match,

226
00:10:29,713 --> 00:10:33,091
but I feel resistance from
the stone I don't experience

227
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:35,385
when using my Quake energy.

228
00:10:35,385 --> 00:10:37,221
You're probably trying to lift.

229
00:10:37,221 --> 00:10:39,139
Earth's power comes from below.

230
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:42,518
Instead of pulling up,
reach down and push out.

231
00:10:42,518 --> 00:10:45,812
[energy zapping]

232
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:49,024
Wow, I never considered
how two similar powers

233
00:10:49,024 --> 00:10:50,317
could be so different.

234
00:10:50,317 --> 00:10:51,735
Thank you, sir!

235
00:10:54,571 --> 00:10:56,532
[Ras groans]

236
00:10:57,741 --> 00:10:59,701
Are you sure it's a good idea

237
00:10:59,701 --> 00:11:02,788
-to help someone on Ras' team?
-You heard what Zane said.

238
00:11:02,788 --> 00:11:05,582
We can't let our past with
Ras color our judgment.

239
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:07,835
I've got a good
feeling about Frak.

240
00:11:07,835 --> 00:11:10,754
Besides, isn't he Arin's friend?

241
00:11:10,754 --> 00:11:13,841
[dramatic music]

242
00:11:13,841 --> 00:11:16,718
[crowd cheering]

243
00:11:18,262 --> 00:11:20,222
[bell tolling]

244
00:11:20,222 --> 00:11:21,974
[Roby] Frak opens strong
with a Quake,

245
00:11:21,974 --> 00:11:24,977
but the Master of
Reflex dodges with ease!

246
00:11:24,977 --> 00:11:28,272
Uh-oh, Zur! Better look
before you leap and after.

247
00:11:28,272 --> 00:11:30,941
We don't call this game
Grid Drop for nothing!

248
00:11:30,941 --> 00:11:33,735
[light zapping]

249
00:11:37,072 --> 00:11:41,159
If that were us up there,
the battle would
already be over.

250
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:44,037
When I was in exile,
all I had was the dream

251
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:48,625
of exacting revenge
on my sister.

252
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:50,752
You Ninja stole
that chance from me.

253
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:56,175
Seems only right to exact
that same revenge on you.

254
00:11:56,175 --> 00:11:58,927
[Ras laughing]

255
00:11:58,927 --> 00:12:00,304
-[groaning]
-[laughing]

256
00:12:00,304 --> 00:12:02,472
This is the Legendary
Green Ninja

257
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:05,058
who dethroned my sister?

258
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:06,810
Sad.

259
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:09,438
-[dramatic music]
-[sighs]

260
00:12:12,816 --> 00:12:15,360
[fist thudding]

261
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:20,490
[light zaps]

262
00:12:23,577 --> 00:12:26,997
-[group gasps]
-Frak, reach down and push out!

263
00:12:26,997 --> 00:12:28,999
[dramatic music]

264
00:12:28,999 --> 00:12:31,627
Yeah!

265
00:12:31,627 --> 00:12:34,171
[light zapping]

266
00:12:39,009 --> 00:12:40,844
[crowd cheering]

267
00:12:40,844 --> 00:12:42,346
[Roby] We have a winner.

268
00:12:45,015 --> 00:12:47,809
[light zapping]

269
00:12:51,855 --> 00:12:55,317
[crowd cheering]

270
00:12:55,317 --> 00:12:58,153
How dare you seek
counsel from the enemy!

271
00:12:58,153 --> 00:12:59,738
What? Master Cole?

272
00:12:59,738 --> 00:13:01,532
Well, it's his power,
I just thought--

273
00:13:01,532 --> 00:13:04,826
Master Cole? I am
your Master, no other.

274
00:13:04,826 --> 00:13:07,454
Do you understand?

275
00:13:08,997 --> 00:13:10,290
Yes, Master.

276
00:13:11,667 --> 00:13:12,918
[gulping]

277
00:13:12,918 --> 00:13:14,795
[coughs] Ugh!

278
00:13:14,795 --> 00:13:17,881
The tea's cold and I've got
no powers to heat it with!

279
00:13:17,881 --> 00:13:21,051
Not having Elemental Powers
is just the worst!

280
00:13:21,051 --> 00:13:23,303
I mean, it's fine
for some people.

281
00:13:23,303 --> 00:13:25,722
Not everyone is suited
for an exciting life.

282
00:13:25,722 --> 00:13:26,890
Oh, hi, Arin!

283
00:13:27,558 --> 00:13:30,435
Wyldfyre, what do
you think of Roby?

284
00:13:32,187 --> 00:13:34,273
He's alright, I guess,

285
00:13:34,273 --> 00:13:37,526
for a super cool genius
that everyone adores.

286
00:13:37,526 --> 00:13:39,653
Why? Did he ask about me?

287
00:13:39,653 --> 00:13:42,072
Just trying to follow the facts.

288
00:13:42,072 --> 00:13:44,199
-[crowd cheering]
-[dramatic music]

289
00:13:44,199 --> 00:13:47,244
-[bell tolls]
-[crowd cheering]

290
00:13:47,244 --> 00:13:49,746
[dramatic music]

291
00:13:51,164 --> 00:13:52,749
[bell tolling]

292
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:54,626
-Yeah! Woo-hoo!
-[cheering]

293
00:14:17,733 --> 00:14:21,278
[water bubbles]

294
00:14:22,154 --> 00:14:24,698
[light zapping]

295
00:14:29,953 --> 00:14:31,705
[crashes]

296
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:34,333
[dramatic music]

297
00:14:40,047 --> 00:14:42,674
[fireball zings]

298
00:14:45,177 --> 00:14:46,970
[crowd cheering]

299
00:14:46,970 --> 00:14:51,934
-[light zapping]
-[dramatic music]

300
00:15:11,662 --> 00:15:12,871
[bell tolls]

301
00:15:12,871 --> 00:15:15,374
[grunts] That was--

302
00:15:15,374 --> 00:15:16,458
A lot.

303
00:15:16,458 --> 00:15:19,002
[sighs] At least it's over.

304
00:15:19,002 --> 00:15:22,256
Guess your vision about fighting
Zeatrix today was wrong.

305
00:15:22,256 --> 00:15:25,008
Well, it's all over for today.

306
00:15:25,008 --> 00:15:27,010
Or is it?

307
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:29,012
Wait, what? Surprise!

308
00:15:29,012 --> 00:15:31,390
Ya boi planned a
secret bonus game.

309
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:33,725
[cheering]

310
00:15:33,725 --> 00:15:36,854
Wow! That's what all your
minds sound like right now!

311
00:15:38,105 --> 00:15:41,358
He's lean, he's green,
but he's never mean.

312
00:15:41,358 --> 00:15:44,027
It's Lloyd, Elemental
Master of Life!

313
00:15:44,027 --> 00:15:49,116
-[crowd cheering]
-His opponent is a former twin,
who will do anything to win.

314
00:15:49,116 --> 00:15:52,703
The very angry Elemental
Master of Shockwave, Zeatrix!

315
00:15:55,330 --> 00:15:58,292
Welcome to The
Gauntlet what-what?

316
00:15:58,292 --> 00:16:00,043
This game's goal is simple.

317
00:16:00,043 --> 00:16:02,045
Retrieve these epic
hand-to-hand weapons

318
00:16:02,045 --> 00:16:04,673
and yeet your opponent
off the platform.

319
00:16:04,673 --> 00:16:06,216
The sword from my vision.

320
00:16:07,426 --> 00:16:09,928
Gotta get to it
before Zeatrix does.

321
00:16:09,928 --> 00:16:11,597
The challengers
are free to use any

322
00:16:11,597 --> 00:16:15,058
and all Elemental Powers,
but the final blow

323
00:16:15,058 --> 00:16:17,936
must be executed with a
weapon from the Gauntlet.

324
00:16:17,936 --> 00:16:19,396
Copy? Cool.

325
00:16:19,396 --> 00:16:22,065
Ready? Set?
Go, go, go.

326
00:16:22,065 --> 00:16:23,775
[bell tolls]

327
00:16:23,775 --> 00:16:26,069
[fire explodes]

328
00:16:26,069 --> 00:16:28,071
Lloyd's coming out hot! Ba-Bam!

329
00:16:28,071 --> 00:16:31,617
-[dramatic music]
-[Lloyd grunts, groans]

330
00:16:31,617 --> 00:16:33,452
Oops, maybe too strong!

331
00:16:33,452 --> 00:16:36,079
Looks like Lloyd hasn't mastered
that elemental power yet!

332
00:16:36,079 --> 00:16:37,539
Can't all be winners!

333
00:16:38,999 --> 00:16:42,085
-[blades breaking]
-Easy breezy.

334
00:16:42,085 --> 00:16:44,880
Zeatrix uses the
Elemental Power of wind.

335
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,132
Be sure to thank
Euphrasia later, Z!

336
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:51,178
[light zapping]

337
00:16:51,178 --> 00:16:53,847
[dramatic music]

338
00:16:53,847 --> 00:16:55,974
[swords clangs]

339
00:16:55,974 --> 00:17:00,020
Elemental Fusion fused
those weapons! Clever move!

340
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:01,355
Look out below!

341
00:17:04,608 --> 00:17:06,610
[light zapping]

342
00:17:06,610 --> 00:17:08,570
Zing! Lloyd uses the
Elemental Power of Size

343
00:17:08,570 --> 00:17:11,156
to duck Zeatrix's blast.

344
00:17:11,156 --> 00:17:14,409
Remember, there are no small
Powers, only small masters.

345
00:17:15,661 --> 00:17:18,580
Lloyd is deploying an
unusual fight strategy.

346
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:21,667
Yeah, it's not fighting.
It's running away.

347
00:17:21,667 --> 00:17:24,711
[dramatic music]

348
00:17:38,475 --> 00:17:41,395
And Zeatrix pulls out the
Elemental Power of Figment!

349
00:17:41,395 --> 00:17:44,189
She's her own party,
but which one is real?

350
00:17:44,189 --> 00:17:48,944
[blows thudding]

351
00:17:48,944 --> 00:17:52,155
Your sister Beatrix didn't
need these tricks to fight me.

352
00:17:52,155 --> 00:17:55,617
No, she needed an army. My army!

353
00:17:55,617 --> 00:17:56,785
Gotcha.

354
00:17:56,785 --> 00:17:59,830
[light zapping]

355
00:17:59,830 --> 00:18:04,209
Ouch! Lloyd Ze-a-tricked her
into giving up
her real location!

356
00:18:04,209 --> 00:18:07,171
[crowd cheering]

357
00:18:07,171 --> 00:18:09,923
[dramatic music]

358
00:18:11,550 --> 00:18:12,843
No!

359
00:18:12,843 --> 00:18:15,387
[light zapping]

360
00:18:16,638 --> 00:18:19,308
[dramatic music]

361
00:18:28,192 --> 00:18:32,487
Blink and you miss it!
Lloyd pulls a Mr. Pale
and goes invisible.

362
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:36,408
-[light zapping]
-[dramatic music]

363
00:18:36,408 --> 00:18:37,701
This could be it!

364
00:18:39,912 --> 00:18:41,914
Why doesn't Lloyd knock her off?

365
00:18:41,914 --> 00:18:45,542
I've got to find that
sword from my visions.

366
00:18:45,542 --> 00:18:47,669
Where did you go, coward?

367
00:18:47,669 --> 00:18:49,922
[dramatic music]

368
00:18:49,922 --> 00:18:53,759
-[light zapping]
-There you are.

369
00:18:53,759 --> 00:18:57,137
Wow! Zeatrix using Elemental
Sound to echolocate.

370
00:18:57,137 --> 00:19:01,266
Folks, I've never seen and
not seen anything like this!

371
00:19:02,643 --> 00:19:04,895
Seems like Zeatrix is
using the Elemental Power

372
00:19:04,895 --> 00:19:08,065
of Surface Tension to fill a
bubble with shockwave energy.

373
00:19:08,065 --> 00:19:10,192
She's making an Elemental Bomb!

374
00:19:13,570 --> 00:19:16,323
[bomb explodes]

375
00:19:18,742 --> 00:19:21,662
-[crowd cheering]
-They've broken the game!

376
00:19:21,662 --> 00:19:24,831
In thousands of years, this
has never happened before!

377
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:27,167
Is my tournament wild or what?

378
00:19:27,167 --> 00:19:29,503
Stang-zooot!

379
00:19:29,503 --> 00:19:32,840
We need a short intermission
while bots repair the Gauntlet

380
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:35,259
from this unprecedented
intensity.

381
00:19:35,259 --> 00:19:36,802
I encourage you to
visit concessions,

382
00:19:36,802 --> 00:19:38,762
hear there's some amazing pies!

383
00:19:41,265 --> 00:19:43,267
You're doing great, buddy.

384
00:19:43,267 --> 00:19:46,270
You have already beaten the
odds by getting this far.

385
00:19:46,270 --> 00:19:49,982
You're losing, Lloyd, but
not to her, to your own fear.

386
00:19:49,982 --> 00:19:54,570
You're right. But how do I fight
a battle I've seen myself lose?

387
00:19:54,570 --> 00:19:57,531
When I faced Cinder, you
told me not to make my fear

388
00:19:57,531 --> 00:20:00,701
a self-fulfilling prophecy.
And I won.

389
00:20:00,701 --> 00:20:03,662
Ninja don't fight because
we know we'll win,

390
00:20:03,662 --> 00:20:08,125
we do it because some things
are worth fighting for,

391
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:09,877
no matter what the outcome is.

392
00:20:11,962 --> 00:20:13,964
Maybe I should
take my own advice.

393
00:20:15,382 --> 00:20:18,260
[dramatic music]

394
00:20:19,344 --> 00:20:22,389
Welcome back, competitors
and spectators.

395
00:20:22,389 --> 00:20:24,516
These games would be
nothing without you.

396
00:20:24,516 --> 00:20:27,019
Well, they'd be just me,
which is still pretty amazing.

397
00:20:27,019 --> 00:20:29,313
But I dare say, enough about me!

398
00:20:29,313 --> 00:20:31,315
[dramatic music]

399
00:20:31,315 --> 00:20:33,692
[bell tolls]

400
00:20:35,068 --> 00:20:37,112
Zeatrix brings back the bubble!

401
00:20:37,112 --> 00:20:40,115
But adding some Elemental
Wind to give herself the edge!

402
00:20:42,117 --> 00:20:44,119
[bubble bursts]

403
00:20:44,119 --> 00:20:46,079
Whoa! I hate to burst
her bubble,

404
00:20:46,079 --> 00:20:47,414
but Lloyd
just burst her bubble!

405
00:20:50,167 --> 00:20:52,127
[Lloyd] No more running.

406
00:20:52,127 --> 00:20:54,796
-[dramatic music]
-[yelling]

407
00:20:56,882 --> 00:21:00,093
[both grunting and yelling]

408
00:21:09,394 --> 00:21:11,396
-[screaming]
-Yes!

409
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:13,982
[crowd cheering]

410
00:21:13,982 --> 00:21:15,526
Lloyd is the winner!

411
00:21:20,405 --> 00:21:21,782
Hey, hey, hey, stop!

412
00:21:21,782 --> 00:21:23,075
The game's already over.

413
00:21:23,075 --> 00:21:24,368
Lloyd, look out!

414
00:21:24,368 --> 00:21:27,329
[dramatic music]

415
00:21:28,372 --> 00:21:30,666
[Ras laughing]

416
00:21:30,666 --> 00:21:32,918
[Lloyd crashes]

417
00:21:33,877 --> 00:21:37,256
[Lloyd groans]

418
00:21:37,256 --> 00:21:39,466
-[dramatic music]
-[gasping]

419
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:46,348
[Lloyd coughs, gasps]

420
00:21:46,348 --> 00:21:49,434
[dramatic music plays]

